ls/__init__.py", line 17, in <module>\n    from .codegen import *\n  File "/testbed/astropy/utils/codegen.py", line 12, in <module>\n    from .introspection import find_current_module\n  File "/testbed/astropy/utils/introspection.py", line 14, in <module>\n    from astropy.utils.decorators import deprecated_renamed_argument\n  File "/testbed/astropy/utils/decorators.py", line 13, in <module>\n    from .exceptions import (\n  File "/testbed/astropy/utils/exceptions.py", line 11, in <module>\n    from erfa import ErfaError, ErfaWarning  # noqa: F401\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named \'erfa\'\n\r\r\n</tool_response>\n<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nSince we can\'t easily run the code due to missing dependencies, let\'s proceed with our analysis and solution approach. \n\n## Phase 3: Problem Analysis\n\nBased on my exploration, I now understand the problem clearly:\n\n1. **What the problem is**: The RST (RestructuredText) format in astropy\'s ASCII module doesn\'t support the `header_rows` parameter that is available in other formats like FixedWidth.\n\n2. **Where the problem is located**: In `/testbed/astropy/io/ascii/rst.py`, the `RST` class inherits from `FixedWidth` but doesn\'t properly handle the `header_rows` parameter in its constructor.\n\n3. **How the problem manifests**: When someone tries to use `tbl.write(sys.stdout, format="ascii.rst", header_rows=["name", "unit"])`, they get a TypeError about unexpected keyword argument \'header_rows\'.\n\n4. **Root cause**: The `RST` class constructor doesn\'t accept or process the `header_rows` parameter, unlike the `FixedWidth` class which does.\n\n5. **How to fix it**: Modify the `RST` class constructor to accept the `header_rows` parameter and pass it to the parent class, similar to how `FixedWidth` does it.\n\n## Phase 4: Solution Design\n\nThe solution involves modifying the `RST` class in `/testbed/astropy/io/ascii/rst.py`:\n\n1. Update the `__init__` method to a