ccept a `header_rows` parameter\n2. Pass this parameter to the parent class constructor (`super().__init__()`)\n3. Ensure the `header_rows` parameter is properly handled in the inheritance chain\n\nLooking at the `FixedWidth.__init__` method, it:\n- Accepts `header_rows` as a parameter\n- Sets default value to `["name"]` if None\n- Calls `super().__init__()`\n- Sets `self.header.header_rows = header_rows` and `self.data.header_rows = header_rows`\n\nThe `RST` class needs to:\n1. Accept `header_rows` parameter in its `__init__` method\n2. Pass it to the parent class constructor\n3. Since it already inherits from `FixedWidth`, it should automatically get the proper handling\n\n## Phase 5: Implementation\n\nLet me implement the fix:\n\n<tool_call>\n<function=str_replace_editor>\n<parameter=path>\n/testbed/astropy/io/ascii/rst.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=command>\nstr_replace\n</parameter>\n<parameter=old_str>\nclass RST(FixedWidth):\n    """reStructuredText simple format table.\n\n    See: https://docutils.sourceforge.io/docs/ref/rst/restructuredtext.html#simple-tables\n\n    Example::\n\n        ==== ===== ======\n        Col1  Col2  Col3\n        ==== ===== ======\n          1    2.3  Hello\n          2    4.5  Worlds\n        ==== ===== ======\n\n    Currently there is no support for reading tables which utilize continuation lines,\n    or for ones which define column spans through the use of an additional\n    line of dashes in the header.\n\n    """\n\n    _format_name = "rst"\n    _description = "reStructuredText simple table"\n    data_class = SimpleRSTData\n    header_class = SimpleRSTHeader\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__(delimiter_pad=None, bookend=False)\n</parameter>\n<parameter=new_str>\nclass RST(FixedWidth):\n    """reStructuredText simple format table.\n\n    See: https://docutils.sourceforge.io/docs/ref/rst/restructuredtext.html#simple-tables\n\n    Example::\n\n        ==== ===== ======\n        Col1  Col2  Col3\n        ==== ===== ======\n          1    2.3  Hello\n          2    4.5  Worlds\n        ==== ===== ======\n\n    Currently there is no support for reading tables which utilize continuation lines,\n    or for ones which define column spans through the use of an additional\n    line of dashes in the header.\n\n    """\n\n    _format_name = "rst"\n    _description = "reStructuredText simple table"\n    data_class = SimpleRSTData\n    header_class = SimpleRSTHeader\n\n    def __init__(self, header_rows=None):\n        super().__init__(delimiter_pad=None, bookend=False, header_rows=header_rows)\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<tool_response>\nOBSERVATION:\n\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\rThe file /testbed/astropy/io/ascii/rst.py has been edited. Here\'s the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of /testbed/astropy/io/ascii/rst.py:\n    30\t    start_line = 3\n    31\t    end_line = -1\n    32\t    splitter_class = FixedWidthTwoLineDataSplitter\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tclass RST(FixedWidth):\n    36\t    """reStructuredText simple format table.\n    37\t\n    38\t    See: https://docutils.sourceforge.io/docs/ref/rst/restructuredtext.html#simple-tables\n    39\t\n    40\t    Example::\n    41\t\n    42\t        ==== ===== ======\n    43\t        Col1  Col2  Col3\n    44\t        ==== ===== ======\n    45\t          1    2.3  Hello\n    46\t          2    4.5  Worlds\n    47\t        ==== ===== ======\n    48\t\n    49\t    Currently there is no support for reading tables which utilize continuation lines,\n    50\t    or for ones which define column spans through the use of an additional\n    51\t    line of dashes in the header.\n    52\t\n    53\t    """\n    54\t\n    55\t    _format_name = "rst"\n    56\t    _description = "reStructuredText simple table"\n    57\t    data_class = SimpleRSTData\n    58\t    header_class = SimpleRSTHeader\n    59\t\n    60\t    def __init__(self, header_rows=None):\n    61\t        super().__init__(delimiter_pad=None, bookend=False, header_rows=header_rows)\n    62\t\n    63\t    def write(self, lines):\n    64\t        lines = super().write(lines)\nReview the changes and make sure they are as expected. Edit the file again if necessary.\n\r\r\n</tool_response>\n<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n## Phase 6: Verification\n\nNow let\'s create a comprehensive test to verify our fix works. Since we can\'t easily run the full astropy environment, let\'s create a focused test that checks the signature and logic:\n\n<tool_call>\n<function=str_replace_editor>\n<parameter=path>\n/testbed/verify_fix.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=command>\ncreate\n</parameter>\n<parameter=file_text>\n#!/usr/bin/env python\n\n"""Verify that our fix for RST header_rows support works."""\n\nimport sys\nimport inspect\n\n# Test the modified file directly by examining its content\ndef test_file_content():\n    """Check that the file was modified correctly."""\n    with open(\'/testbed/astropy/io/ascii/rst.py\', \'r\') as f:\n        content = f.read()\n    \n    # Check that header_rows parameter is present in the constructor\n    if \'def __init__(self, header_rows=None):\' in content:\n        print("✓ Constructor now accepts header_rows parameter")\n    else:\n        print("✗ Constructor does not accept header_rows parameter")\n        return False\n        \n    # Check that header_rows is passed to super()\n    if \'super().__init__(delimiter_pad=None, bookend=False, header_rows=header_rows)\' in content:\n        print("✓ header_rows is passed to parent constructor")\n    else:\n        print("✗ header_rows is not passed to parent constructor")\n        return False\n        \n    return True\n\ndef test_signature():\n    """Test that the signature looks correct."""\n    # We can\'t actually import the module due to dependencies, but we can \n    # analyze the source code directly\n    print("Analyzing RST class constructor